  {
    "episode_id": 51093,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51093.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Senator, what differentiates tech from a normal multinational conglomerate? So like general electric, for example. So like general electric gets the light bulb patent, then all of a sudden in the mid 2000s, they become a financial services company, a light bulb company, also a washing machine company, also that. So is it the objection to a conglomeration of a business? Like why is technology in these firms that you're talking about specifically different, given that we've had Semi-similar companies in America for almost 100 years now.",
