    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "It's interesting, Senator, because this is, you know, we were asking the clubhouse example and the Twitter example as well. How do you balance competition? I'm channeling, you know, what I think some of the more libertarian critics in us have messaged us as saying like, listen, you know, Twitter, there have been many examples of dynamic industries. AOL actually just this week, I think sold for $5 billion at one point, literally acquired all of Time Warner. And that happened within the span of 20 years. So how does the legislation and just your general thinking balance the ability to maintain dynamism as a company? Because you can be big and fall. That's the story of some parts of the internet while also wanting to balance competition.",
