    "turn_text": "Something I wonder about is how much of this conversation is frozen in the years 2015 through 2017 in the sense that obviously the three of us are no fans of TikTok. But the one side part of the TikTok conversation is that Facebook was actually scared of TikTok because you actually have an outside player who outcompeted them when it came to actually creating a platform that young people actually wanted to use. So you have TikTok, you have the rise of clubhouse, you have venture capitalists actually putting money into the social media sector, newly, probably during the pandemic going on that way. So how do you just think about how the narrative is shifting there? Do you think it's a real narrative or is this a whole we shouldn't wait and see in five years dynamic?",
