    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 51093,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51093.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think because this is where the American people are. At the end of the day, I think what the American people want is control over their own lives. They want to be able to raise their own families, not have big tech do it. And they don't want these companies to have this kind of power. They don't want to see the monopoly status and the monopoly politics continue. And I think ultimately, what do elected officials, what do politicians respond to? Ultimately, they respond to their voters. And I think that's why you've seen Republicans tone change on this in the last two years. It's changed a lot since I've been in the Senate. And that hasn't been very long. That's only been two years.",
